WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.490 --> 00:00:03.655
A key file for your cloud account sits in a Secret.

2
00:00:03.675 --> 00:00:05.330
It is valid for years.

3
00:00:05.350 --> 00:00:08.140
And it works from any machine that has a copy.

4
00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:14.040
This port has two ideas: the identity of a pod, and cloud access with no keys.

5
00:00:14.060 --> 00:00:16.750
First: every pod has an identity.

6
00:00:16.770 --> 00:00:19.050
A pod runs as a service account.

7
00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:21.735
The node gives it a token for that account.

8
00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:25.970
The token lives for about an hour, and stops when the pod is deleted.

9
00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.557
The token says who you are.

10
00:00:27.577 --> 00:00:30.770
Access control decides what you may do.

11
00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:33.530
Second: reach the cloud with no key file.

12
00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:36.305
The cloud trusts the service account of the cluster.

13
00:00:36.325 --> 00:00:38.090
You grant a role to it.

14
00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:40.802
The pod gets a short cloud token when it asks.

15
00:00:40.822 --> 00:00:44.140
Nothing to store, nothing to rotate.

16
00:00:44.160 --> 00:00:46.200
Quick recap of identity.

17
00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:47.900
One service account per app.

18
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.275
Tokens are short-lived.

19
00:00:49.295 --> 00:00:51.085
And no key files.

20
00:00:51.105 --> 00:00:54.205
Now start the first lesson below.
